// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/t27f/petal_specs_viz.t27 -- petal 18 (S SPECS), the reference petal of the interactive
; visualization epic (issue #12174, epic #12173). Built on specs/t27f/viz_contract.t27.
; --
; What it answers: "how does a value spread through this spec's graph, layer by layer?" The reader
; selects a node (the seed), steps through the layers, picks how neighbours are combined (sum, mean
; or max) and switches single edges off to watch the spread change. This is the t27 reading of the
; Distill GNN introduction (distill.pub/2021/gnn-intro): one graph, several linked views, an input
; to change and the intermediate steps shown, here on a REAL spec graph and not on a toy.
; --
; Data source: tutorial_08_graph() of specs/t27f/spec_graph.t27, the graph of
; specs/tutorial/08_modules_and_arrays.t27 (15 nodes, 16 edges). spec_graph_derive.t27 proves it
; equal to the exporter's output on that file, so the petal opens with truth VIZ_TRUTH_VERIFIED.
; Switching an edge off is a what-if on that graph, not a fact about the file: the petal then shows
; VIZ_TRUTH_DEMO and (viz_may_claim) may not present its numbers as a result until every edge is
; on again. A reload keeps the DEMO label while any edge is off.
; --
; Layers of this spec:
;   L1 state       PsvState = one VizState (the contract's) + an edge mask; psv_apply forwards every
;                  contract event to the one reducer viz_apply and adds ONE petal event, the toggle.
;   L2 entities    node i = viz_ref(NODE, i), edge j = viz_ref(EDGE, j), matrix cell (i, j) =
;                  viz_ref(CELL, i * 16 + j); the focus order is nodes 0..14, then edges 0..15.
;   L3 adjacency   undirected and boolean: two nodes are adjacent when any ENABLED edge joins them,
;                  in either direction. The parallel edges of the fixture (a `uses` and a
;                  `data_flow` edge between one pair) count once, and switching off only one of a
;                  parallel pair leaves the pair adjacent.
;   L4 passing     layer 0 = the seed holds PSV_SEED, every other node 0; layer k+1 of node v =
;                  aggregate of the layer-k values of v itself and of every neighbour of v, by
;                  integer sum, floor mean, or max. PSV_LAYERS rounds, so a trace holds 5 layers.
;   L5 oracle      psv_hops: breadth-first distance over the edge list, written apart from the
;                  message passing. A node holds a value at layer k exactly when it is within k hops
;                  of the seed; the tests check that for every seed, aggregation, layer and node.
;   L6 views       graph (the real spec_graph_view boxes), matrix (15 x 15 cells) and list (one
;                  line per edge): each has a layout function and an inverse hit test, and all three
;                  read the ONE VizState through viz_highlight plus a relation rule (RELATED).
;   L7 inspector   everything about the node under the pointer (else the seed): its lines in the
;                  real spec, degree, value at the current step and aggregation, hops from the seed.
;   L8 host        psv_host: nested VizHost slots for the frame, badge, choice, stepper, graph,
;                  matrix, list, trace and inspector; psv_reps is the set of reps it uses.
; --
; Integer only: no floats, `/` and `%`, features u64. Pixel geometry is in frame coordinates (the
; origin is the frame's top-left corner), so a hit test and psv_host agree without an offset.
; --
; Limits: at most 16 nodes and 16 edges are read (the mask is one u32, a trace row is 16 slots).
; --
;   L9 host map   what a host needs and must not decide: pack and unpack of the state into six u64
;                  words, the fit of the frame into a page and its inverse, the hit tests of the
;                  controls, a click, hover and key map to events, and the trace shading.
; --
; The host is the SPECS page of specs/t27os/glass_window.t27 (issue #12199). It maps pointer and key
; events to the L9 functions, calls psv_apply, and draws boxes, lines, cells, list lines, trace
; values, inspector lines and the truth badge from the answers of the layers above; it holds no
; viz logic of its own. Not claimed: no run of the app on a screen is recorded in this file.

